{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Jump take-off",
  "description": "A runner in trainers jumping straight up from a wooden gym floor: the crouch loads the boards for 60 ms with a creak-less push (a soft double thump as heel then toe leave, 0 and 45 ms), the soles scuff grit as they twist off, and the body goes up through its own clothes with a short rising rush of air from 50 to 300 ms. No cartoon boing: the effort is in the push.",
